WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A reference workspace for creators, players and developers.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Five sections keep worlds, saves, community, avatars and transfers together.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Choose a local or API model using OpenAI, Responses or Anthropic protocols.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Adjust structured output, temperature compatibility and context budget.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Test the saved connection with an actual model request. Waiting is shortened.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Read the returned result before creating a world.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Describe a world and its first story. Choose scale and content language.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Optionally bind a prepared 2D NPC. This portrait came from an imported package.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:48.000
The engine creates content and automatically playtests it. Waiting is shortened.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Each tested revision reports structure, mechanics, model play and content review.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:16.000
Edit, retest, request AI text repair or export a native story.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:28.000
World settings and stories are separate versioned objects.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Inspect places and their connections in the location editor.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Edit NPC personality, goals, knowledge and optional portrait bindings.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Story overview, acts, clues, challenges and systems have their own tabs.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Create another story in the same world from a new idea.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:31.000
Both stories use the same world and retain their own test reports.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Start a tested story with your own player character.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Write a natural-language action or dialogue. Model waiting is shortened.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:15.000
The 2D NPC performs committed dialogue with expression and motion.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:31.000
Read narration and state effects together after the action commits.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Record a personal note or commitment without advancing world time.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:55.000
Search known memories and inspect their source records.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:07.000
Fork at an earlier turn to explore another direction.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:19.000
Branches retain their own events and memories.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:35.000
This imported revision failed content review. Inspect the reported claim before repair.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:51.000
AI text repair creates a new revision and reruns the automatic checks.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:06:03.000
An imported RPG example adds equipment, commerce and combat rules.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:15.000
Inspect structured item and rule definitions in the world editor.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:30.000
The Actions tab exposes legal operations and current resources.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:42.000
Select a rule action directly; the engine validates its preconditions.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:57.000
Committed rule changes and narration remain in the same event history.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:09.000
Open the map when you need routes and world context.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:25.000
A living-world example tracks offscreen characters and faction progress.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:37.000
Pause or resume world simulation from the player interface.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:53.000
Buy from a shop: inventory and coins change together in one committed action.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:08:09.000
Follow connected map routes to reach the encounter.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:25.000
Choose an attack and let the configured rule system resolve combat.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Inspect the recorded dice, modifier, threshold and outcome. Replay keeps this result.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:57.000
Define variables, visibility, conditions, actions, triggers and authored test routes.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:12.000
Only player-visible values and available actions appear in the game view.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:24.000
Create a shared-character or independent-character multiplayer room.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:40.000
A second browser joins as Alex with an independent character.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:56.000
Room tools group player views, notes, character control and trades.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:08.000
The host submits a conversation in the shared room. Model waiting is shortened.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:24.000
Room narration reflects the committed world version and participating characters.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:36.000
Choose a previous campaign as continuity for the next story.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:48.000
Package tested stories with creator credit, license and optional 2D assets.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:11:00.000
Download a portable native package from your community shelf.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:12.000
Inspect included stories before installing and automatically testing a copy.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Export the full campaign, including its branches and event history.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:36.000
Preview a backup before restoring it as an independent adventure.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:48.000
Install the exported package as an editable copy. Waiting for testing is shortened.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:12:04.000
The copied world and both stories have their own automatic test results.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:16.000
Restore the validated backup into a new campaign.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:32.000
The restored campaign keeps its branches and committed history.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:44.000
Assign a provider and model separately for each engine module.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:56.000
Module descriptions explain which model abilities each task needs.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:08.000
Configuration example: a System One decision model in shadow mode; unsaved.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:20.000
Configuration example: a separate embedding model for hybrid memory; unsaved.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:32.000
Inspect calls, reported tokens and optional price estimates by model.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:52.000
Actual SDK result: access the same world library without the reference UI.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:14:12.000
Executed fixture example: custom action modules, replay, forks and restoration.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Actual model evaluation: frozen tasks, assertions, latency and token accounting.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:52.000
Executed fixture example: checkpointed trajectories, resume and recall checks.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:15:07.000
Switch the interface language while authored world and story text stays intact.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:21.000
Build with the backend, SDK, reference UI and guides at github.com/Toyhom/NarraLoom.
